  "recipes": {
    "cli/command-design": {
      "description": "Principles for designing command-line interfaces in any language: inferring intent and defaulting sensibly, informed consent over prevention, safe and non-interactive behavior, consistent flag naming and flag grammar, network and remote reads, plan-then-confirm execution, and plain factual output, with action skills for creating a new command and for updating an existing one.",
