    "communication/agent-conduct": {
      "description": "Always-loaded conduct rules for an agent working with a person: a question is not an instruction, solve the whole problem, keep durable memories in tracked sources, quote a source's exact words behind every assertion based on what it said, label every rule it writes as a ruling or an inference and read unsourced rules as tentative, respect the user's time (research before asking, no hangers, links, numbered points, one report), show a requested draft in chat instead of sending it, and take outward actions (pushes, pull requests, merges, releases, issues, comments, messages) only as far as this project's settings allow; plus partials for quoting, rulings and provenance, replying to questions, and reporting back, and the /create-reply command, which drafts replies that quote each question before answering it.",
